{#
  Why signing in needs cookies.

  **Rendered by no route.** It is what `/user/login` and `/user/verify` answer with when the
  visitor has not consented, through JUser\Page\CookieExplainer — at the requested URL, with
  a 200, rather than by redirecting. A redirect would rewrite the address bar of someone who
  had just clicked an emailed link, and the point is that the link is still good once they
  consent: the token is spent only on a successful redemption.

  There is deliberately no route for this page and there should not be one. On
  schoenstatt.link, where it came from, `/sign-in-no-cookies` existed for years with **no
  guard entry** — so default deny made the URL unreachable from the day it was written, and
  the only thing that ever showed the page was a laminas route-match swap running at
  priority -5000, i.e. after the guard had already approved a *different* route. The page
  rendered without ever being authorized. It was deleted from both front controllers on
  2026-08-21 and cost nothing, because the swap built its match by hand and named no route.

  Two faithful oddities, carried over rather than fixed, because the evidence that this port
  changed nothing is a byte-for-byte diff of the rendered page:

  - **the `<h1>` is "Sign In" and the sign-in page's is "Sign in".** Two separate phrases in
    the translation table, and the consuming application's smoke tests use that difference
    to tell which of the two pages they are looking at.
  - **the paragraph is not translated.** The .phtml printed it as a raw English literal with
    no `translate()` around it, so a visitor who has refused cookies reads English whatever
    their locale. Left alone deliberately: fixing it puts a new phrase in the table, which
    is a change to make on its own rather than inside a port.

  The .phtml set no `headTitle()`, so the page title is passed **empty**. Absent would be a
  fatal on a layout that reads `page_title` unguarded under `strict_variables` — and such a
  fatal arrives as a 200 with an empty body rather than as a 500.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Sign In') }}</h1>

<p class="text-danger">Warning, without consenting to using cookies on this website, there is no way to sign in. Please accept consent, and <strong>reload the page</strong>.</p>
{% endblock %}
